394	// ============================================================================
395	// §5  AMD-NATIVE device kernels (Stage 5 hand-written AMDGCN attention).
396	//
397	// This section is the REAL hand-written gfx942 forward+backward, built on the
398	// shared, compiler-verified primitives in
399	//   csrc/backends/hip/gfx942/amdgcn_primitives.hip.hpp   (namespace amd = …).
400	//
401	// It is compiled ONLY by an AMDGCN device pass:
402	//   * the Stage-5 device-compile gate  (scripts/amdgcn_check.sh, __AMDGCN__), and
403	//   * the hipcc device pass             (__HIPCC__ on a real ROCm build).
404	// The host `.hip.cpp` TU never sees it — that pass keeps the ATen orchestration
405	// above (which LAUNCHES these kernels via hipLaunchKernelGGL, see §5.LAUNCH).
406	//
407	// Self-contained on purpose: under the free-standing gate the only reachable
408	// headers are the amdgcn_primitives stub set (no <cmath>/<cstdint>/bfloat16),
409	// so the model math here uses clang __builtin_* (valid under hipcc too) and a
410	// local bf16<->f32 bit codec rather than common_gfx942.hip.hpp's host helpers.
411	//
412	// HARDWARE-GATED 🟡: device-compile-verified for gfx942 only; MI300X numerics +
413	// rocprof MFMA-utilization are deferred (HARDWARE_VALIDATION.md, Stage 5).
414	//
415	// ── §2.10 LDS scratchpad sizing for the 64 KB CDNA3 budget ───────────────────
416	// The sm_90 FMHA reference stages whole K/V head tiles in 228 KB SMEM. CDNA3 has
417	// only 64 KB LDS/CU, so the attention tiling here is sized to the grokking
418	// shapes (d_head D=32, seq_len N ∈ {4,17}; one wavefront per (batch,head)):
419	//   * scores S[N×N]   : N≤32 → ≤ 32*32*4 B = 4096 B
420	//   * row_max[N]      : ≤ 32*4 B = 128 B   (DPP-reduced, see softmax below)
421	//   * row_sum[N]      : ≤ 32*4 B = 128 B
422	//   TOTAL ≤ 4352 B  ≪ 65536 B  — fits comfortably, no K/V re-tiling needed.
423	// For larger N a flash-style streaming tile would cap the score buffer at
424	// (N × Bc) with Bc the K/V block (e.g. Bc=64 → 64*32*4 = 8 KB), keeping LDS
425	// under the 64 KB budget; the grokking shapes don't reach that regime.
426	// ============================================================================
