2579	// ── §5.ADAM  per-element AdamW apply (128-bit / f32x4 vectorized) ─────────────
2580	// The standalone elementwise apply tail of the MoE/Adam multi-tensor path
2581	// (launch_moe_adam_step). Lives in sg::gfx942::native (matching the MoE
2582	// compaction kernels + the host forward-decl). BIT-IDENTICAL to the ATen host
2583	// path (primitives.hpp ema_update_inplace / ema_sq_update_inplace /
2584	// adam_apply_inplace):
2585	//   m   = beta1*m + (1-beta1)*g
2586	//   v   = beta2*v + (1-beta2)*g*g
2587	//   m_hat = m/bc1 ; v_hat = v/bc2 ; denom = sqrt(v_hat)+eps
2588	//   p  -= lr*(m_hat/denom + wd*p)
2589	// Memory access widens to 128-bit dwordx4 (f32x4 streaming_load/streaming_store
2590	// on param/exp_avg/exp_avg_sq/grad); the scalar tail runs the identical math on
2591	// the n%4 remainder. Per-lane math, order, constants and __builtin_sqrtf are
2592	// unchanged from the scalar form — only the access width changes.
2593	//
2594	// SCOPE: this is the ONLY cleanly-vectorizable elementwise apply in SG2. The
2595	// CSA/HCA single-param apply tail (sg2_step_one_param, §(8)-(10)) is FUSED into
2596	// the per-parameter attention/GRU/PEER pipeline (its smart_grad depends on the
2597	// per-row GRU output gru_new[:,0] and uses the coupled-WD form p*=(1-lr*wd)) —
2598	// it is matmul/structured-fused, NOT a standalone elementwise kernel, so it
2599	// stays on the ATen host path. The attention MFMA, PEER, GRU and softmax-DPP
2600	// device kernels are matmul/reduction-shaped and are left untouched.
2601	namespace sg { namespace gfx942 { namespace native {
2602	namespace amd_apply = ::sg::gfx942::amdgcn;
2603	using f32x4 = ::sg::gfx942::amdgcn::f32x4;
